    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42-a2">

                <pb facs="0116" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg42"/>

                <head>Count Bismarck to Mr.
                        Wright.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 9, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: From the enclosed letters you had been
                    good enough to communicate to me, I see the contributors to that munificent
                    donation of ice, which has been sent successively from Hamburg for our
                    hospitals, include a considerable number of your countrymen.</p>
                <p>The war office has already conveyed to the committee the thanks of his Majesty’s
                    government for the patriotic feeling which prompted the gift, and for the
                    inestimable benefit conferred upon our wounded soldiers. It becomes my pleasant
                    duty to add the expression of my sentiments of deep gratification at the active
                    sympathy evinced by citizens of the United States with our struggle, which,
                    undertaken for the defence of our homes, will, under God’s blessing, secure the
                    condition to Germany of national life, and to Europe of lasting peace.</p>
                <p>Believe me, dear sir, yours, very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Y. BISMARCK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph A. Wright,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
